          {
            "heading": "",
            "text": "Emotional intelligence at work means noticing your own feelings, managing your reactions, understanding what others need and handling relationships well, and it can be practised through small habits such as pausing before replying, asking questions and giving specific feedback."
          },
          {
            "heading": "",
            "text": "Practise one habit at a time, such as a pause before responding, and gather feedback from a trusted colleague on how it lands."
          },
          {
            "heading": "",
            "text": "If stress affects your daily life, speak to a qualified professional."
          }
        ]
      },
